- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests`

**How to implement.** The Data step reviews one experiment's points, and a point is excluded with a reason, or taken back, by semantic messages that write the experiment file (001 §P `ExcludePoint`; 001 §O 'Data dialog: … per-point exclusion with a reason'; 001 §K 'Raw data is immutable'; .spec-md §4 'UI': every user step is a semantic message; .spec-md §10.5: an exclusion is taken back by `IncludePoint`, its undo). The views that send them are step 325's. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3: (1) Before the model: `ReviewedData = { experimentId : Experiments.ExperimentId; points : Result<MappedPoints, ExperimentDataError> }`, the experiment the Data step reviews and every point of its data as read, the excluded ones included, so that they stay visible; and `DataStepDraft = { exclusionReason : ControlCaption; correctionNote : ControlCaption }`, the texts of the Data step's two fields, with `static member empty : DataStepDraft` (both blank). `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `reviewedDataOpt : ReviewedData option` and `dataDraft : DataStepDraft`, each with a one-line doc; `initWith` sets `None` and `DataStepDraft.empty`. (2) Messages, each documented in one line: `ReviewExperimentData of Experiments.ExperimentId` (review an experiment's data): for an experiment the collection holds, `reviewedDataOpt` becomes `Some { experimentId; points }` with `points` = `model.experimentData.readMapped data` (step 305) for its `dataOpt = Some data`, and `Error (EmptyDataFileErr "<name> has no data file")` for `None`; an experiment the collection lacks changes nothing. It reads and writes nothing else, so a read-only kit reviews too. `SetExclusionReason of ControlCaption` sets `dataDraft.exclusionReason`, writing nothing. `ExcludePoint of Experiments.ExperimentId * MappedPointNumber * ControlCaption` (exclude that point of the experiment's data for that reason) and `IncludePoint of Experiments.ExperimentId * MappedPointNumber` (take the point's exclusion back) are each refused by the read-only guard of step 185, which every write message calls. (3) `ExcludePoint (id, point, reason)`: an experiment the collection lacks changes nothing; a reason `ExclusionReason.tryCreate` refuses sets `kitStatus` to `Not excluded — an exclusion needs a reason.`; an experiment with no data `Not excluded — <name> has no data file.`; a `readMapped data` error `Not excluded — <e.caption>`; a point above the read points' `pointCount` `Not excluded — <name> has <n> point(s).`; each of these writes nothing. Otherwise the experiment whose `dataOpt` is `Some (data.withExclusion { point; reason })` (step 313) is recorded through `KitLibraryContext.recordExperiment` (step 261): on `Ok` the collection takes it (`withStoredExperiment`, step 294), its badge is computed again by the one private validation function (steps 136, 295), `reviewedDataOpt` is read again when it reviews this experiment, and `kitStatus` is `Excluded point <n> of <name>: <reason>.`; on `Error e` the model is kept with `kitStatus` `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. `IncludePoint (id, point)`: an experiment the collection lacks, or whose data holds no exclusion of that point, changes nothing and writes nothing; otherwise `data.withoutExclusion point` is recorded and taken the same way, with `kitStatus` `Included point <n> of <name> again.`. Neither message changes the lab file, the attachment, the profile or the row selection. No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `ExperimentModelTests` (step 292), over its folder kit with `E1` committed over the polarizer's R1 with the draft's range 0…90° and a test-local intensity file `angle_deg,intensity\n0,1.0\n45,0.5\n90,0.0\n` written outside the kit attached by `AttachDataFile (ExperimentId 1, <it>, ImportProfileName.intensitySeries)`: `reviewing an experiment's data reads every point, the excluded ones included, and writes nothing`: `ReviewExperimentData (ExperimentId 1)` leaves `reviewedDataOpt` holding E1 and `Ok (SeriesPoints _)` of three points, and every file's bytes unchanged; after `ExcludePoint (ExperimentId 1, MappedPointNumber 2, ControlCaption "beam blocked")` it still holds three points; `ReviewExperimentData (ExperimentId 9)` changes nothing. `ExcludePoint records a point's exclusion and its reason in the experiment file, and IncludePoint takes it back`: that `ExcludePoint` leaves E1's data excluding point 2 for `beam blocked`, the `E1.experiment-json` read back through `readExperiments` holding the same, the attached file's bytes unchanged, `model.dataBadgeOf E1` `ExcludedPointsBadge (2, 1)` and `kitStatus` `Excluded point 2 of E1: beam blocked.`; then `IncludePoint (ExperimentId 1, MappedPointNumber 2)` leaves no exclusion in the model and the file, the badge `ValidatedDataBadge` of 3 points, and a second `IncludePoint` writes nothing. `an exclusion without a reason, of a point the data lacks, or of an experiment without data writes nothing`: `ExcludePoint` with the reason `"  "`, of point 4, and of `E2` (committed with no data) each set the `kitStatus` above and leave every file's bytes unchanged. `KitWindowModelTests` (steps 185, 294, 310): `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` also sends `ExcludePoint` and `IncludePoint`, with its assertions.

**Acceptance.** After the review and exclusion messages land, `ReviewExperimentData` MUST read every point of an experiment's data and write nothing, `ExcludePoint` MUST record a point's exclusion with its non-blank reason in the experiment file and `IncludePoint` take it back, each refused typed for a blank reason, a point the data lacks, an experiment without data and a read-only kit, the lab file never changing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `reviewing an experiment's data reads every point, the excluded ones included, and writes nothing`, `ExcludePoint records a point's exclusion and its reason in the experiment file, and IncludePoint takes it back` and `an exclusion without a reason, of a point the data lacks, or of an experiment without data writes nothing`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.
